@startuml SD08_Calibration
!include _style.iuml
title SD-08  Calibrate lens and define the working area (UC-12, UC-13) — REQ-19 … REQ-22, REQ-47, REQ-57

actor Imager
participant ":SettingsViewModel" as SVM
participant ":FrameTimeReader" as Time
participant ":ImageViewerWindow\n(Calibration mode)" as View
participant ":CalibrationViewModel" as CVM
participant ":LensCalibrationSession" as Sess
participant ":StarDetector" as Det
participant ":InitialGuessSearch" as Srch
participant ":LensFitter" as Fit
participant ":CalibrationQualityCheck" as Q
participant ":PluginSettingsStore" as Store

Imager -> SVM : Calibrate from a frame…\n(allsky-20261020022133.jpg)
SVM -> Time : FromFileName(name, local time zone)
Time --> SVM : 2026-10-19 15:21:33 UTC
note right of SVM : No time in the name → message under the\ncalibration buttons; no window opens.\n"Calibrate from current image" uses the\nimage's recorded capture time instead.
SVM -> View ** : open(CalibrationFrame)
Imager -> View : Fit
View -> CVM : FitCommand
CVM -> Sess : Calibrate(frame, site)
activate Sess
Sess -> Det : Detect(frame)
Det --> Sess : ~2,500 spots (hot pixels removed)
Sess -> Srch : Search(spots, frame, site, utc)
alt pattern found
  Srch --> Sess : starting lens model
else no convincing match
  Srch --> Sess : none
  Sess --> CVM : NeedsIdentification
  CVM --> View : "Click two or three named stars"
  Imager -> View : pick "Canopus", click it; "Achernar", click; "Rigel", click
  View -> CVM : StarIdentification ×3
  CVM -> Sess : CalibrateFromIdentified(frame, site, picks)
  Sess -> Sess : starting model from the picks
end
Sess -> Fit : Fit(spots, start, site, utc)
Fit -> Fit : match catalogue stars (mag ≤ 4.5) within 25 → 6 px,\nleast squares on centre, rotation, c1..c3, reject outliers
Fit --> Sess : LensFitResult (33 stars, 2.7 px, 0.15°)
Sess -> Q : Warnings(result)
Q --> Sess : none (warn if < 15 stars or > 0.2°, REQ-20)
deactivate Sess
Sess --> CVM : CalibrationOutcome
CVM --> View : overlay: catalogue circles + alt/az grid (REQ-21),\nresult text and any warnings
Imager -> View : inspect by eye (zoom, pan)
Imager -> View : Draw outline: click around trees,\nhouse and overlay text (REQ-22)
Imager -> View : Save
View -> CVM : SaveCommand
CVM -> Store : Save(Calibration.Lens, Calibration.WorkingArea.Outline)
note right of Store : JSON settings (REQ-57). The running monitor\nuses them from its next cycle. Cancel, or an\noutside click, never closes Calibration mode.
@enduml
